I'm getting an unaligned access error message in my program.
Unfortunately it only occurs when `-O2' is specified. I therefore had
to compile with `-O2 -g3' in order to debug it, but the location it
reports the unaligned access is in a call to memcpy and there does not
seem to be a way to access the value of locals and arguments. The line
of code looks like:

memcpy (dest, &i, sizeof(int));

where `dest' is a char *, most likely unaligned since it is an
arbitrary memory area.
where `i' is an argument passed to the function in which `memcpy' is
called.

Any hint on how to solve this,
